## Rule ATLASSIAN.3: Extra official commands (not basic retrieval)

Basic `view` + `search` covers ticket fetch for bug validation, cross-dependency, test cases, Phoenix Q&A, regression validation, and Slack Jira context.

These official commands are allowed **only** for the bug-reporter flow (Rule PHOENIX-BUG.0), after the review file is `# Bug Review — APPROVED` and `.active-bugreview` is written:

```bash
acli jira project list --limit 50 --json
acli jira workitem create --from-json payload.json --json
acli jira workitem edit --key KEY-123 --from-json payload.json --yes --json
```

`project list --paginate` is allowed only when the first page does not contain the project the user must pick. Do not create projects, fields, or bulk work items. Do not delete attachments, comments, or links.

There is **no** official createmeta command. For a bug-reporter project, read issue types and versions with `acli jira project view --key KEY --json`. Ask the user only when the needed type name is absent, or when a required version was not chosen yet. Do not guess Epic or custom-field ids. Do not fall back to Jira REST createmeta.

---

## Rule ATLASSIAN.4: Confluence GET only

Same credentials as today (`JIRA_EMAIL`, `JIRA_API_TOKEN`, or `CONFLUENCE_EMAIL` / `CONFLUENCE_API_TOKEN`, wiki base `CONFLUENCE_WIKI_BASE`). Never print the token.

**One page:**

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "Cursor-Project/config/confluence/get-confluence-page-rest.ps1" -PageId "<numericId>"
```

**CQL search** (bug validation and cross-dependency only; other flows stay on linked page IDs — Rule 39):

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "Cursor-Project/config/confluence/search-confluence-cql-rest.ps1" -Cql "<cql>" -Limit 25
```

`-Limit` maximum **50**. Read full page JSON for hits you cite. Do not POST, PUT, or DELETE.

**Chat line:** `Confluence source: Cloud REST GET.`

